{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ErrorPresentation","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/errorpresentation"]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Error Presentation"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Error presentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Error-presentation"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything the default Error placeholders do beyond showing a generic icon and message: telling a connectivity problem apart from everything else, an optional second action alongside Retry, and a user-facing message distinct from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizedDescription"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the one state whose presentation can’t be fully generic — a timed-out request, a missing article, and a malformed response all deserve different words, and sometimes a different action, even though they’re all just an "},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". This article rounds up the three pieces "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" use to narrow that gap without you writing a fully custom placeholder."}]},{"anchor":"The-offline-aware-variant","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The offline-aware variant"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/isConnectivityError(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" for a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLError"},{"type":"text","text":" indicating no network connectivity ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".notConnectedToInternet"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".networkConnectionLost"},{"type":"text","text":") or a timed-out request ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".timedOut"},{"type":"text","text":"). When it’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", the default Error placeholders swap their usual warning-triangle icon and “Something Went Wrong” title for a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wifi.exclamationmark"},{"type":"text","text":" icon and “Connection Issue” instead — the same distinction a fully custom placeholder can make with the same check:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["if ScreenState<Never>.isConnectivityError(error) {","    \/\/ show your own offline-specific treatment","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every other error, including other "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLError"},{"type":"text","text":" codes, falls back to the generic treatment."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-secondary-action-slot","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The secondary action slot"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both default Error placeholders take an optional "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"secondaryAction: (title: String, action: () -> Void)?"},{"type":"text","text":" alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" — a second button for something other than retrying, like going back to the previous screen instead of hammering a request that’s going to fail the same way again:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateDefaultErrorView(error: error, onRetry: reload, secondaryAction: (title: \"Go Back\", action: goBack))","ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView(error: error, onRetry: reload, secondaryAction: (title: \"Go Back\", action: goBack))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" by default, so every existing call site keeps showing just Retry (or nothing, if "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" is also "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":") until you opt in."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-user-facing-message-distinct-from-localizedDescription","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"A user-facing message, distinct from localizedDescription"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error.localizedDescription"},{"type":"text","text":" is often a debugging string, or — for a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedError"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance — just the type name,